  "repairs": [
    "Ten typed statement forms transport declaration-pass order, DML target-column order, rel roots, types, function declarations, catalog identity and frozen metadata without parsing SQL on import.",
    "Generated statements retain the exact parser input through AST rewrites. Explicit source contexts prevent internal identifier coordinates from being validated against unrelated user SQL.",
    "Catalog values and relation uses retain their evaluation source context; Rust rejects missing sources, mismatched catalog/value contexts, missing nullable fields and invalid statement ownership.",
    "Catalog schemas are captured before lowering mutates column metadata and reconstructed declarations share mutable columns with their catalog objects.",
    "External aggregate metadata includes qualified name positions, parameter/return types and the linear flag. Reconstruction retains declaration/call operator object identity.",
    "This snapshot includes the parsed FLOOR diagnostic fix and the DML target-column permutation fix. Their production prefix comparison is a separate check."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The imported stream is reconstructed and structurally checked, but has not yet been fed into detached S1-to-S2 lowering. No S1 parity claim.",
    "The operator arena is shared by declarations, scalar calls and relational aggregate calls. Focused Java/Rust fixtures cover called and uncalled external aggregates; the positive corpus does not establish coverage of every supported declaration form.",
    "Multi-batch compilation, complete compiler context and diagnostic interleaving, JDBC tables and join system-field metadata remain open.",
    "Independent reviews, staffing decisions and other P0 exit gates remain open."
  ]
}
